# .gitignore — plaintext-labs
# These labs run tools (tcpdump, openssl, volatility, metasploit, prowler, …) that emit
# captures, keys, dumps and logs. Small curated seed data under data/ is committed on
# purpose; the heavy/dangerous artifacts below never are — labs download or generate them.

# === Secrets — never commit ===
.env
.env.*
*.pem
# Exception: a curated, KEYLESS, already-expired sample cert is committed on
# purpose as deterministic offline seed data for the cert-expiry lab.
!foundations/01-security-principles/sample-expired-cert.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ed25519
*.kdbx
*.token
credentials

# === Generated lab artifacts: captures, memory/disk images, logs ===
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.cap
*.pcap.zip
# Track 09: downloaded PCAP archives and large Suricata-generated corpora — labs
# fetch/generate these (small curated eve.json seeds under data/ ARE committed on purpose).
python-for-security/*/_gen/
*.log
*.dmp
*.mem
*.vmem
*.raw
*.lime
*.img
*.E01
*.aff4

# === Malware samples — keep out of the repo entirely ===
samples/
*.malware

# === Python tooling ===
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# === PowerShell lab artifacts (Track 13) — event exports, signing certs, secret stores ===
*.evtx
*.pfx
*.p7s
*.clixml
PowerShell_transcript*
localstore/
*.secretstore
.sign/

# === OS / editor cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# shared dataset cache (lib/fetch.sh)
.cache/

# transient raw feed snapshots staged by `make refresh` (the committed snapshot is feeds/db.json)
python-for-security/*/feeds/feodo.json
python-for-security/*/feeds/urlhaus.csv
